# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed — this is a deployed app (not a template), so
# builds are reproducible and the Docker image builds with `--locked`.

# Trunk / WASM build output
leptos-app/dist/
*.wasm

# Local config: ignore only the akdev-managed root patch. Nested .cargo dirs
# (e.g. leptos-app/.cargo/config.toml, which carries wasm build flags) are kept,
# and so is `.cargo/audit.toml` — cargo-audit reads its ignore list from that
# exact path, so the CI advisory gate needs it committed. The `/*` + negation
# spelling is required: git cannot re-include a file under an excluded
# directory, so the directory itself must stay un-excluded.
/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/audit.toml

# e2e (Playwright). The lockfile is COMMITTED on purpose: the e2e job gates
# production deploys, so the browser tooling it runs must not float.
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/test-results/

# Dev runner (local, per-checkout state)
.dev-ports
.dev-pid
.dev-log

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Secrets — never commit private keys. The dev JWT signing key is in-memory
# only (prod uses ANKURAH_JWT_SIGNING_KEY from Secret Manager), but guard against
# any local key material regardless. `.p8` is the extension Apple issues an APNs
# signing key under; the server reads that key from APNS_KEY_P8, so a copy in
# the tree is only ever an accident.
*.pem
*.p8
signing-key*
leptos-app/Trunk.dev.toml
# The same rendered proxy table, written by e2e/playwright.config.ts for a test
# run rather than by dev.sh for a dev session (port-named: concurrent runs must
# not clobber each other's).
leptos-app/Trunk.e2e.*.toml

# The pre-rename generated file: briefly committed by accident, never generated again.
leptos-app/Trunk.e2e.toml
